  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&#x200B;&#x200B;Support for procurement of chronic medications and Trauma advanced kits and hospitalization coverage in response to the escalation of hostiles in South Lebanon &#x200B;</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to deliver life-saving medical interventions in the areas affected by the ongoing hostilities in south Lebanon. Activities will include provision of financial coverage for life and limb-saving medical care in Baalbek-Hermel, Bekaa, South and Nabatiyeh, provision of chronic medication to primary health care facilities, and procurement of trauma and emergency surgery kits (TESK). Under the Health cluster, this project will support 110,523 individuals, including 60,582 women, 1,265 children, and 2,110 persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
